The created new modules are appended to the standardized module pools {P, R, T, M} and each module is used to individually mutate the initial agent, resulting in N child agents {A 1 e , A 2 e , ..., A N e }. For example, (P * , R 0 , T 0 , M 0 ) represents a solution where the planning module is mutated into a new variant P * . These child agents are then real-tested and updated to the historical experience pool E. The best-performing one is selected as the initial agent for the subsequent recombination phase.

